  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nInterest earned during the 2ⁿd year = Rs. 2761\n\nRate of interest = 10%\n\n**Concept Used:**\n\nCI = P(1 + (r/100))² - P(1 + (r/100))\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nCI = P(1 + (r/100))2 - P(1 + (r/100))\n\nCI = P(1 + (r/100)) [(1 + (r/100)) - 1]\n\n⇒ 2761 = P(1 + (10/100)) [(1 + (10/100)) - 1]\n\n⇒ 2761 = P(1 + (1/10)) [(1 + (1/10)) - 1]\n\n⇒ 2761 = P(11/10)(1/10)\n\n⇒ P = (2761 × 10 × 10)/11\n\n⇒ P = 25100\n\n**The sum is Rs. 25100.**\n\n**∴ Option 3 is the correct answer.**",
